From: genshanxinli <127909456+genshanxinli@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: refuse an HFWD ring the queue cannot hold

airoha_qdma_init_hfwd_queues() writes num_desc into the 17-bit
HW_FWD_DESC_NUM_MASK field without bounds checks, silently truncating
oversized reserved-memory regions or accepting zero descriptors. Reject
num_desc == 0 or num_desc > HW_FWD_DESC_NUM_MASK with -EINVAL.

Origin: archive/xr1710g-v1@e85677d284c0
Signed-off-by: genshanxinli <127909456+genshanxinli@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -1575,6 +1575,12 @@ static int airoha_qdma_init_hfwd_queues(
 		 * reserved memory size and the payload buffer size
 		 */
 		num_desc = div_u64(rmem->size, buf_size);
+		if (!num_desc || num_desc > HW_FWD_DESC_NUM_MASK) {
+			dev_err(eth->dev,
+				"%s needs %d descriptors, only 1-%lu fit\n",
+				name, num_desc, HW_FWD_DESC_NUM_MASK);
+			return -EINVAL;
+		}
 	} else {
 		size = buf_size * num_desc;
 		if (!dmam_alloc_coherent(eth->dev, size, &dma_addr,
